    {
      "id": "web_of_science_1630",
      "title": "Quantifying the Greenhouse Gas Emissions in the Construction of Wooden School Structures Using the Cross-laminated Timber Construction Method",
      "authors": "Fuchigami, Yuki and Watanabe, Kenta and Nakai, Takahisa",
      "affiliations": "Mie University",
      "countries": [],
      "journal": "MOKUZAI GAKKAISHI",
      "year": 2020,
      "score": 29,
      "abstract": "The volume of greenhouse gases (GHGs) emitted during the process from product manufacturing step to the construction process in the life cycle of a wooden school building (two stories: total floor area: 407.2 m(2)) constructed using cross-laminated timber (CLT) was quantified. GHG emissions were also quantified for school buildings with a reinforced concrete structure (hereafter, ``RC structure''",
