      "year": 2016,
      "score": 32,
      "abstract": "Cross Laminated Timber (CLT) is currently used in modern timber structures for load-bearing wall, floor or roof elements as a high quality, innovative and cost-effective structural element. Careful planning and implementation ensures the safe use of CLT in buildings with increased fire protection requirements and in accordance with the requirements of building-design standards (e. g. EN 1995-1-1 and EN 1995-1-2) [",
