    {
      "id": "web_of_science_1532",
      "title": "Full-Scale Cross-Laminated Timber Diaphragm Evaluation. I: Design and Full-Scale Diaphragm Testing",
      "authors": "Line, Philip and Nyseth, Scott and Waltz, Ned",
      "affiliations": "Line, P (Corresponding Author), Amer Wood Council, Struct Engn, 222 Catoctin Circle SE Suite 201, Leesburg, VA 20175 USA. Line, Philip, Amer Wood Council, Struct Engn, 222 Catoctin Circle SE Suite 201, Leesburg, VA 20175 USA. Nyseth, Scott, 2001 NW 19th Ave,STE 103A, Portland, OR 97209 USA. Waltz, Ned, Weyerhaeuser, Prod Evaluat \\& Performance, POB 6049, Federal Way, WA 98063 USA.",
      "countries": [],
      "journal": "JOURNAL OF STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING",
      "year": 2022,
      "score": 45,
      "abstract": "The objective of this study was to monotonically test two 7.32x7.32-m (24x24-ft) cross-laminated timber (CLT) diaphragms designed using the provisions of ANSI/AWC 2021 (AWC. 2021. Special design provisions for wind and seismic. ANSI/AWC SDPWS-2021, Leesburg, VA: AWC). Each diaphragm used twelve 1.22x3.66-m (4x12-ft) CLT panels and plywood splines or glulam beams at panel shear connection locations. Diaphragms were tested in simple-span bending in general accordance with ASTM E455 (ASTM. 2017. Standard test method for static load testing of framed floor and roof diaphragm constructions for buildings. ASTM E455-2017. West Conshohocken, PA: ASTM), used 8d common [",
