    {
      "id": "web_of_science_1527",
      "title": "Two-hour Fireproof Performance of Cross Laminated Timber (CLT) Covered with Fire-retardant Impregnated Wood",
      "authors": "Harada, Toshiro and Kamikawa, Daisuke and Miyatake, Atsushi and Shindo, Kenta and Hattori, Nobuaki and Ando, Keisuke and Miyabayashi, Masayuki",
      "affiliations": "Forestry \\& Forest Products Research Institute - Japan; Tokyo University of Agriculture \\& Technology",
      "countries": [
        "Japan"
      ],
      "journal": "MOKUZAI GAKKAISHI",
      "year": 2019,
      "score": 54,
      "abstract": "In order to develop 2-hour-fireproof cross laminated timber (CLT) floor and wall structures, covering them with wood impregnated with fire-retardant agent was studied. In the fire test of the CLT wall specimen, two layers of fire-retardant impregnated wood (Cryptomeria japonica D. Don) were alternately laminated with screws to the load-bearing CLT and a fire test was conducted for 2 hours. The total thickness of the covering material was 90 mm. However, the CLT burned due to early drop-off of the top layer and shrinkage of the second layer, and the wall specimen did not show 2-hour fire resistance performance. Based on this test result, in the fire test of the floor, the covering material was specified as a fire-retardant impregnated wood panel of three layers of 30 mm thick treated wood and a 10 mm thick untreated wood layer laminated and bonded together with adhesives. The panels were joined by two types of spline made of fire-retardant impregnated wood, and were attached to the CLT with screws. The screw holes were filled with untreated wood. In the 2 hour-fire tests of the floor specimens, flames died out and charring stopped in the covering layer. This result shows that covering with fire-retardant impregnated wood panels makes the CLT 2-hour fireproof.",
      "keywords": [
        "two-hour fireproof",
        "CLT",
        "fire retardant",
        "flame die-out",
        "drill incising"
      ],
      "studyType": "Article",
      "quality": null,
