    {
      "id": "web_of_science_1314",
      "title": "Evaluating Laboratory Measurements for Sound Insulation of Cross-Laminated Timber (CLT) Floors: Configurations in Lightweight Buildings",
      "authors": "Vardaxis, Nikolaos-Georgios and Hagberg, Delphine Bard and Dahlstrom, Jessica",
      "affiliations": "Lund University",
      "countries": [],
      "journal": "APPLIED SCIENCES-BASEL",
      "year": 2022,
      "score": 63,
      "abstract": "Cross-laminated timber (CLT) floors with supplementary layers or floating floors comprise a common solution in new multistory timber structures. However, bare CLT components provide poor sound insulation, especially in low frequencies during structure-borne sound propagation. Thus, floor configurations in wooden buildings deploy more layers for improved acoustic behavior. Twelve contemporary CLT floors were analyzed after laboratory measurements of airborne sound reduction and impact sound transmission utilizing the following indicators: R-w, R-w,R- 100, R-w,R- 50, L-n,L-w, L-n,L-w,L-100, and L-n,L-w,L-50 (per ISO 10140, ISO 717). An increase in sound insulation was achieved thanks to added total mass and thickness, testing layers of the following: elastic mat for vibration isolation, wool insulation, gypsum boards, plywood, concrete screed, and wooden parquet floor. The results indicate that multilayered CLT floors can provide improvements of up to 22 dB for airborne sound and 32 dB for impact sound indicators compared with the bare CLT slab. Floating floor configurations with dry floor solutions (concrete screed) and wooden parquet floors stand out as the optimal cases. The parquet floor provides a 1-2 dB improvement only for impact sound indicators in floating floor setups (or higher in three cases).",
      "keywords": [
        "cross-laminated timber",
        "airborne sound",
        "impact noise",
        "sound insulation",
        "timber"
      ],
      "studyType": "Article",
      "quality": null,
      "doi": "10.3390/app12157642",
      "language": "English",
