    {
      "id": "scopus_786",
      "title": "Assessment of structural interventions using Bayesian updating and subspace-based fault detection methods: the case study of S. Maria di Collemaggio basilica, L’Aquila, Italy",
      "authors": "Aloisio, Angelo and Di Battista, Luca and Alaggio, Rocco and Antonacci, Elena and Fragiacomo, Massimo",
      "affiliations": "Università degli Studi dell'Aquila, Department of Civil, L'Aquila, AQ, Italy; Università degli Studi dell'Aquila, Department of Information Engineering, Computer Science and Mathematics, L'Aquila, AQ, Italy",
      "countries": [
        "Italy"
      ],
      "journal": "Structure and Infrastructure Engineering",
      "year": 2021,
      "score": 6,
      "abstract": "The article focuses on the assessment of a structural intervention using a simple Bayesian approach driven by subspace-based indicators. A permanent monitoring system installed in a monumental masonry structure, the basilica of Santa Maria di Collemaggio in L’Aquila Italy, continuously acquires vibration data. The results of modal identification are first reported and discussed. Then, the article delivers a damage detection procedure, tested on two sets of data measured by the façade accelerometers before and after the CLT (Cross-Lam Timber) roof connection, which are interpreted as damage and reference states, respectively. The application of Bayesian inference to a set of damage indicators for the assessment of the façade structural modification is presented and compared with the results of a non-parametric (Formula presented.) -tests. A computation procedure for the built of a statistical reference model is proposed by discussing the issue of the choice of the reference data set. © 2020 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.",
      "keywords": [
        "Damage assessment",
        "dynamic tests",
        "earthquake engineering",
        "masonry",
        "risk and probability analysis"
      ],
      "studyType": "Article",
      "quality": null,
      "doi": "10.1080/15732479.2020.1731559",
      "language": "English",
