      "journal": "ASTM Special Technical Publication",
      "year": 2017,
      "score": 6,
      "abstract": "The proceedings contain 19 papers. The topics discussed include: analysis of improved criteria for mold growth in ASHREA standard 160 by comparison with field observations; development of standards to evaluate, analyze, and retrofit mass wall assemblies and steep sloped roof assemblies of existing buildings for compliance with energy codes; hygrothermal impact of adhesive-applied rooftop photovoltaic system; comparing the enclosure wall performance of low-permeance exterior insulation to high-permeance exterior insulation in the Pacific northwest; application of VIPs in Canada's north-monitoring results; sensitivity analysis of hygrothermal performance of cross-laminated timber wall assemblies; demonstration of the hygrothermal performance of a next-generation insulation material in a cold climate; sensitivity analysis of moisture-dependent properties of roofing materials; modeling of aerogel blanket insulation applications in exterior wall constructions; hygrothermal performance assessment of stucco-clad wood frame walls having vented and ventilated drainage cavities; three-dimensional condensation risk analysis of insulated curtain wall spandrels; and using hygrothermal modeling to resolve practical low-slope roofing issues.",
