    {
      "id": "scopus_1210",
      "title": "Fire Safety Science",
      "authors": "Autor não informado",
      "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
      "countries": "País não informado",
      "journal": "Fire Safety Science",
      "year": 2014,
      "score": 6,
      "abstract": "The proceedings contain 111 papers. The topics discussed include: enclosure and facade fires: physics and applications; effects of sample width and sidewalls on downward flame spread over XPS slabs; feasibility of particle imaging velocimetry in cone calorimeter experiments; modeling of the pyrolysis of plywood exposed to heat fluxes under cone calorimeter; ignition temperature and surface emissivity of heterogeneous loosely packed materials from pyrometric measurements; real fire test on concrete columns and post-tensioned slabs; an experimental investigation of structural fire behavior of a rigid steel frame; parametric analysis of heat transfer in gypsum wallboard partitions; fire tests on loaded cross-laminated timber wall and floor elements; effective stress method to be used in beam finite elements to take local instabilities into account; a comparison of an explicit and an implicit transient strain formulation for concrete in fire; and simplified calculation for fire performance of post-tensioned timber box beams.",
