    {
      "id": "scopus_544",
      "title": "8th International Conference on Structural Engineering, Mechanics and Computation, SEMC 2022",
      "authors": "Autor não informado",
      "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
      "countries": "País não informado",
      "journal": "Current Perspectives and New Directions in Mechanics, Modelling and Design of Structural Systems - Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Structural Engineering, Mechanics and Computation, 2022",
      "year": 2023,
      "score": 9,
      "abstract": "The proceedings contain 332 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Structural Engineering, Mechanics and Computation. The topics include: In-test analytical model updating for accurate hybrid dynamic simulations; value of vibration-based structural monitoring for bridge emergency management; understanding tensegrity with an energy function; bridge flutter and how to prevent it at low cost; early assessment of the vibroacoustic performance of large lightweight buildings; Modal analysis of CLT beams: Measurements and predictive simulations; optimal design of viscoelastic tuned mass dampers for structures exposed to coloured excitations; numerical investigation on train-bridge interaction after ship impact event: Train running safety in different scenarios; Research advancement on Submerged Floating Tunnels: Recent activity at DICA-Politecnico di Milano; the influence of near-surface soil layer resonance on vibrations in pile foundations; prediction of flutter velocity of long-span bridges using probabilistic approach; the effect of pile slip on underwater noise emission in vibratory pile driving; dynamic analysis of highly symmetric cable dome structures; vibroacoustic performance of multi-storey buildings: A comparison of lightweight and heavy structures in the early design phase; effect of modelling the air in rooms on the prediction of vibration transmission in cross-laminated timber buildings; Numerical analysis of transversely isotropic unsaturated railway ground vibrations under a moving load using 2.5D FEM; incremental dynamic analysis of a hospital building in Oman; dynamic response of parabolic reflector antenna subjected to shock load and base excitation considering soil-structure interaction; effect of Cape storms on the flat roof-mounted solar panels; recent advances in tsunami design of coastal structures.",
