    {
      "id": "scopus_13",
      "title": "6th Central European Symposium on Building Physics, CESBP 2025",
      "authors": "Autor não informado",
      "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
      "countries": "País não informado",
      "journal": "Lecture Notes in Civil Engineering",
      "year": 2026,
      "score": 12,
      "abstract": "The proceedings contain 84 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Building Physics. The topics include: Internal Insulation Systems with Smart Vapour Retarders: Hygrothermal Performance Across European Climates; impacts of Representative Weather Data Type on Hygrothermal Simulations for Future Climate; performance Metric Function for Improving Hygrothermal Calculation Models; coupled Heat and Moisture Transport Simulation of Hungarian Historical Wall-Slab Connections; hygrothermal Modelling Approaches for the Moisture Buffering Behaviour of 3D-Printed Building Components with Complex Geometry; impact of Gaps at the Insulation Joints on the Hygrothermal Performance of Wooden Basements; effect of Subfreezing Relative Humidity Calculation Methods on Simulation Accuracy and Mold Risk in Cold Climates; 2D Hygrothermal Simulations of Cross-Laminated Timber Wall Assemblies Under Rainwater Penetration Conditions; from Single-Scale to Full-Scale: Complete Pore Structure Characterization of Porous Building Materials; hygrothermal Performance of Double-Insulated External Thermal Insulation Component System; simulation of Hygrothermal Behavior of Wood Flooring with Floor Cooling Systems in Present and Future Climate Scenarios; crack Size in Thermally Modified vs. Native Norway Spruce Window Frames: A Comparative Hygrothermal Simulation Study of Moisture Damage; hygrothermal Properties of Mural Painting Materials in Grotto Temples: Implications for Environmental Control in Preventative Conservation; inverse Uncertainty Analysis to Predict Indeterministic Building Design Parameters Based on Detailed Energy Measurements in Hot Climates; development of a Methodology for Hygrothermal Testing Using a Modified Guarded Hot Box; surface Temperatures on the Glazing and Their Influence on the Heat Flux in the Built-In Window; Monitoring Moisture Performance of CLT Exterior Wall Constructions in a Residential Building; preface.",
