    {
      "id": "scopus_356",
      "title": "Evaluating the measurement of the velocity level difference for building constructions which combine Type A and Type B elements",
      "authors": "Mahn, Jeffrey P. and Skoda, Sabrina and Cunha, Iara B. and Müller-Trapet, Markus",
      "affiliations": "National Research Council Canada, Ottawa, ON, Canada",
      "countries": [
        "Canada"
      ],
      "journal": "53rd International Congress and Exposition on Noise Control Engineering, Internoise 2024",
      "year": 2024,
      "score": 13,
      "abstract": "As part of an ongoing research project in the newfour-room flanking facility at the National Research Council Canada, the velocity level differences between cross-laminated timber floors/ceilings and lightweight timber framed walls have been measured according to the standard, ISO 10848-1. The apparent sound reduction indices between the pairs of rooms have also been measured according to ISO 10848-1. The measured apparent sound reduction indices are compared to those predicted according to the standard, ISO 12354-1 based on the measured velocity level differences, the resonant transmission losses and the dimensions of the elements of the flanking paths between the room pairs. © © 2024 by Societe Francaise d'Acoustique All rights reserved.",
