    {
      "id": "scopus_746",
      "title": "Design and construction of a timber building for apartments, library and offices in Norway",
      "authors": "Sánchez-Solís, Manuel and Mo, Gaute and Rando, Mario and Overton, Katie and Ibáñez, Fernando",
      "affiliations": "Degree of Freedom SLU, Valencia, Spain; Degree of Freedom, Oslo, Norway",
      "countries": [
        "Spain",
        "Norway"
      ],
      "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2021, WCTE 2021",
      "year": 2021,
      "score": 16,
      "abstract": "Degree of Freedom, in collaboration with Helen & Hard architects, have designed a four-storey building containing a library, apartments and offices for a bank in Nord Odal, Norway. The construction of the concrete basement and three storeys of timber framed structure is already opened to the public. Glued laminated timber portal frames, with moment resisting corner connections, are placed radially around a central courtyard giving the building its distinctive circular geometry. CLT panels are used for floor slabs, bearing walls and for the communication and services cores, providing lateral stability to the structure. LVL Baubuche timber is also used to stiffen the library beams. All timber elements are shaped in coordination with the architects and fabricated with openings by means of a fully integrated BIM system. © WCTE 2021. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Beech",
        "BIM",
