    {
      "id": "scopus_830",
      "title": "On the hygrothermal behavior of coconuts fiber insulators on green roofs",
      "authors": "Fabbri, Kristian and Tronchin, Lamberto and Barbieri, Fabrizio and Merli, Francesca and Manfren, Massimiliano and La Gennusa, Maria and Peri, Giorgia and Cirrincione, Laura and Panzera, Maria Francesca",
      "affiliations": "Alma Mater Studiorum Università di Bologna, Cesena, Department of Architecture, Cesena, FC, Italy; University of Southampton, Sustainable Energy Research Group, Southampton, Hampshire, United Kingdom; Università degli Studi di Palermo, Department of Engineering, Palermo, PA, Italy; Università degli Studi di Reggio Calabria, Department of Civil, Energy, Environmental and Materials Engineering, Reggio Calabria, RC, Italy",
      "countries": [
        "Italy",
        "United Kingdom"
      ],
      "journal": "Proceedings - 2020 IEEE International Conference on Environment and Electrical Engineering and 2020 IEEE Industrial and Commercial Power Systems Europe, EEEIC / I and CPS Europe 2020",
      "year": 2020,
      "score": 16,
      "abstract": "Coconut fibre insulators, represent an insulating material considered as 'exotic', which clashes with the doubts of his thermo-hygrometric behavior, in particular, in the case of covering technology such as green roofs, a technological solution adopted in the case of sustainable buildings or nearly zero energy building. Green roofs represent a valid constructive solution with high thermal performances, adopted in existing and new buildings. The purpose of the research regards the study of the thermo-hygrometric behavior of the concrete and Cross-Laminated Timber (CLT) slabs, insulated with coconut fibre-boards (CF) such as alternative synthetic insulators, referred to 10 different green roofs scenarios. The results show that coconut fibre insulations are equally comparable to natural and synthetic materials, and their doubts for their applications, also in the green roofs, are related to technological solutions for the implementation in the market and their diffusion between the buildings materials. © 2020 IEEE.",
      "keywords": [
        "coconuts fibre",
        "green roof",
        "moisture",
        "thermal insulation"
      ],
      "studyType": "Conference paper",
      "quality": null,
