      "id": "scopus_154",
      "title": "DPG MEDIA HEADQUARTERS IN AMSTERDAM: A SHOWCASE OF TIMBER-CONCRETE COMPOSITE FLOOR TECHNOLOGY",
      "authors": "Sohier, Luc and Néron, Laurane and Hargot, Benoît",
      "affiliations": "WOW Engineering, Brussels, Belgium",
      "countries": [
        "Belgium"
      ],
      "journal": "Proceedings from the 14th World Conference on Timber Engineering: Advancing Timber for the Future Built Environment, WCTE 2025",
      "year": 2025,
      "score": 17,
      "abstract": "The new DPG Media headquarters in Amsterdam represents a significant advancement in composite structures, showcasing the innovative use of Timber-Concrete Composite (TCC) floors within a hybrid timber structure. This project demonstrates how timber and concrete can achieve enhanced structural performance, improved acoustic properties, and greater span capabilities. Despite challenges like handling creep and shrinkage, applying pre-camber, and extensive time for connector installation, the project successfully provided a modern, flexible, and sustainable workspace. These insights underline the importance of meticulous planning and optimization in hybrid construction, making TCC floors a perfect alternative to fully concrete floors. © (2025) WORLD CONFERENCE ON TIMBER ENGINEERING 2025 (WCTE 2025) All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "CLT",
        "Hybrid Timber Structures",
        "Timber-Concrete Composite"
      ],
      "studyType": "Conference paper",
