    {
      "id": "scopus_350",
      "title": "TRIAL SEISMIC DESIGN FOR 10-STORY TIMBER CONSTRUCTION IN HIGH SEISMIC COUNTRY JAPAN",
      "authors": "Tsuchimoto, Takahiro and Miyake, Tatsuya and Mitushashi, A.",
      "affiliations": "Building Research Institute, Tsukuba, Ibaraki, Japan; Nihon System Sekkei Architects and Engineers, Tokyo, Japan; Ltd., MisawaHomes Institute of Research and Development Fo., Tokyo, Aichi 4820018, Japan",
      "countries": [
        "Japan"
      ],
      "journal": "World Conference on Earthquake Engineering proceedings",
      "year": 2024,
      "score": 19,
      "abstract": "Promoting the use of wood is now one of Japan's most important national policies. After the enforcement of The Act for Wood Use Promotion in Public Buildings in 2010 (renamed as The Act for Wood Use Promotion to Contribute Realization of Carbon-Free Society at 2021), the rate of timber construction based on floor area has improved. However, the rate of increase in the rate of timber construction for mid-and high-rise buildings and non-residential buildings has been slow. Therefore, with the support of the Public/Private R&D Investment Strategic Expansion Program (PRISM) of the Cabinet Office, the trial designs of high-rise wooden building were carried out. In this report, the technical development that were carried out during the trial design of 10-story apartment houses using the mass timber construction and using composite components consist of wood adhesive panels and structural glued laminated timber and design contents of them were reported. For the mass timber construction, it was concluded that using H-beams for horizontal members is efficient, based on various studies. In addition, sleeve pipe joints were used to joint CLT panels of upper and lower stories and between the CLT panel and the steel beams. For the structure consist of composite components with the wooden adhesive panels and the structural glued laminated timber, the optimum structural method was found by parametric tests such as the capacity additivity law of the adhesive panel and the glued laminated timber and the joint specification of them. Applying the structural calculation of the horizontal load-carrying capacity method required for the structural design of buildings over 31 m in height according to Japanese building code to the both construction and structure, the whole collapse mode based on pushover analysis was confirmed, and the ultimate guarantee of joints and members were designed. As a result, we concluded that the structural design of 10-story apartment houses can be completed for the both construction and structure. © 2024, International Association for Earthquake Engineering. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Adhesive joints",
        "Apartment houses",
        "Building components",
        "Concretes",
        "Mortar",
        "Office buildings",
        "Seismic design",
        "Steel beams and girders",
        "Structural analysis",
        "Structural panels",
        "Tall buildings",
