    {
      "id": "scopus_1047",
      "title": "15th International Conference on Structures under Shock and Impact, SUSI 2018",
      "authors": "Autor não informado",
      "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
      "countries": "País não informado",
      "journal": "WIT Transactions on the Built Environment",
      "year": 2018,
      "score": 21,
      "abstract": "The proceedings contain 24 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Structures under Shock and Impact. The topics include: A scaled air blast model for high altitudes; modeling the impact of explosions in enclosed spaces using discontinuous boundary elements and finite volume methods; blast testing of energy absorbing connectors for blast resistant design; experimental tests on personal safety devices for falls from height; quantifying the response of steel columns to multi-axis long-duration blast and thermal loading; study on suppression of the dynamic behavior of collision bulge of lead tube driven by sliding detonation; experimental analysis on reduced-scale protective doors; blast effects and damage characterization on reinforced masonry walls at full-scale; towards a single degree of freedom (Sdof) model for predicting blast performance of cross-laminated timber; sensitivity study of airplane impact on an underground radioactive waste-storage building; analysis of effect of momentum on the behavior of rc beams under low velocity impact loading; a numerical analysis on flat-shaped rc beams under falling-weight impact loading; investigation of local behavior by impact of projectile for reinforced concrete panels; experimental testing of reinforced concrete slabs retrofitted with cfrp and mechanical anchors; risk assessment criteria for machine tools subjected to large earthquake hazards: A proposal; earthquake response of an open-type wharf with a pneumatic caisson foundation; approaches for the calculation of rayleigh damping coefficients for a time–history analysis; analytical investigation of seismic performance of masonry walls strengthened with strain hardening fiber reinforced geopolymer matrix; ballistic performance of enhanced cross-laminated timber (Eclt).",
