    {
      "id": "scopus_470",
      "title": "AN ANALYTICAL MODEL TO INVESTIGATE THE EFFECT OF DIAPHRAGMS ON THE ELASTIC BEHAVIOUR OF MULTI-STOREY COUPLED-PANEL CLT SHEARWALLS",
      "authors": "Oliveira, Damian and Mikael, Ali and Casagrande, Daniele and Doudak, Ghasan",
      "affiliations": "Canadian Wood Council, Ottawa, ON, Canada; Consiglio Nazionale delle Ricerche, Rome, RM, Italy; University of Ottawa, Ottawa, ON, Canada",
      "countries": [
        "Canada",
        "Italy"
      ],
      "journal": "13th World Conference on Timber Engineering, WCTE 2023",
      "year": 2023,
      "score": 26,
      "abstract": "This study develops an analytical model to describe the behaviour of multi-storey multi-panel CLT shearwalls, specifically accounting for cumulative loads between storeys and the effect of the diaphragm. The analysis considers the contribution of hold-downs, wall-to-floor connections, and panel-to-panel joints, as well as loads transferred from storeys above. The analysis has been developed for shearwalls acting as a series of coupled panels (CP) each individually rotating about a corner. Force transfer between storeys is implemented by distributing reactions through the upper floor diaphragm and a direct force from the upper storey's hold-down. Structuring the equations this way allows for a simplified formulation while including several components of the system's complex behaviour. Two-dimensional finite element modelling is used to verify the accuracy of the developed model. © 13th World Conference on Timber Engineering, WCTE 2023. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "CLT",
        "Derivation",
        "Diaphragm Effect",
        "Earthquake",
        "Lateral Design",
        "Mid-rise",
        "Modelling"
      ],
      "studyType": "Conference paper",
      "quality": null,
