    {
      "id": "scopus_770",
      "title": "Development of prefabricated modular bearing system based on the CLT for multi-storey buildings",
      "authors": "Kanócz, Ján and Javoríková, Miroslava and Bajzecerová, Viktória and Mihal'ák, Michal",
      "affiliations": "Technická Univerzita v Košiciach, Department of Architecture, Kosice, Kosice Region, Slovakia; Technická Univerzita v Košiciach, Institute of Structural Engineering, Kosice, Kosice Region, Slovakia",
      "countries": [
        "Slovakia"
      ],
      "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2021, WCTE 2021",
      "year": 2021,
      "score": 26,
      "abstract": "In this paper, the results of the development of a new prefabricated modular wooden bearing structure of multi-storey building from cross-laminated timber are presented. The spatial basic element of bearing structure created from CLT sheets is described. The paper is also focused on the architectural investigation of different layout variations and a suitable spatial arrangement of the bearing structure. The theoretical and experimental investigations are focused on the prototype structure with timber-concrete two-way flat floor plate. In the frame of theoretical investigation results of static and vibration analysis of prototype structure are presented. © WCTE 2021. All rights reserved.",
