    {
      "id": "scopus_2075",
      "title": "Simulation of bending test, tensile test and impact behavior of CFNonwovens in epoxy resin",
      "authors": "Mankiewicz, Jasmin and Frej, Haithem Bel Haj and Cleve, Ernst and Heber, Michael and Gutmann, Jochen Stefan",
      "affiliations": "Hochschule Niederrhein, Institute for Coatings and Surface Chemistry, Krefeld, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany; Ecole Nationale d'Ingenieurs de Monastir, Monastir, Monastir, Tunisia; Universität Duisburg-Essen, Faculty of Chemistry, Duisburg, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany",
      "countries": [
        "Germany",
        "Tunisia"
      ],
      "journal": "Annual Technical Conference - ANTEC, Conference Proceedings",
      "year": 2018,
      "score": 26,
      "abstract": "Currently the CF market increases intensely. 10-30% valuable CF waste is produced during the process by offcuts or by end-of-life parts. Due to new recycling methods the CF is regained from CFRP in chopped form. A reasonable re-use is only given by manufacturing a fiber mat. One example for further processing is an isotropic fleece by wet-laid process. Produced fleeces are impregnated with thermosets by resin transfer molding (RTM). For the thermosets with virgin fibers several fiber length (separated and mixed), as well as different fiber volume fraction were tested and interrelate with specific values (tensile strength, flexural stiffness, YOUNG'S modulus). To design applications with this new material, not only the mechanical properties have to be forecasted. Hence the isotropic fleece is simulated with AUTODESK HELIUS COMPOSITE 2017 by using the classical lamination theory (CLT). © 2018 Society of Plastics Engineers. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Elastic moduli",
        "Elastomers",
        "Epoxy resins",
        "Fibers",
        "Plastic products",
        "Tensile strength",
        "Tensile testing",
