    {
      "id": "scopus_110",
      "title": "02-028-Design of a timber structure for an office building located in a seismic zone, consisting of two storeys; Diseño de estructura de madera de un edificio de oficinas en zona sísmica formado por planta baja y dos alturas",
      "authors": "Gato Carrión, Martín and Olmos Noguera, José Manuel",
      "affiliations": "Universidad Politecnica de Cartagena, Cartagena, Murcia, Spain",
      "countries": [
        "Spain"
      ],
      "journal": "Proceedings from the International Congress on Project Management and Engineering",
      "year": 2025,
      "score": 28,
      "abstract": "The construction sector in building faces challenges due to the need to industrialize processes and reduce its carbon footprint, which boosts the use of new materials such as crossed-laminated timber (CLT). This work transforms the conventional reinforced concrete design of an office building (ground floor and two storeys) to a wood-based one with CLT panels, glulam beams and pillars (GLT). The structural design was performed using software such as CLT Toolbox, Sofistik and self generated code in Matlab to analyze particular failure modes in CLT elements. The results highlight the importance of treating the material with an orthotropic Mindlin-Reissner matrix and properly modeling the stiffness of the joints, reducing maximum stresses by up to three times. In addition, the use of Matlab to evaluate elements automatically and globally using Sofistik data is validated. Although the wooden design increases the initial costs, they are compensated by the incorporation of partitions and environmental impacts. This comprehensive approach establishes a methodology for designing more sustainable structures using prefabricated wooden elements, thereby laying the groundwork for more efficient and environmentally friendly construction practices. © 2025 by the authors.",
      "keywords": [
        "CLT",
        "Open source",
        "Sofistik",
        "Structures",
        "Sustainable"
      ],
      "studyType": "Conference paper",
      "quality": null,
      "doi": null,
      "language": "English",
