    {
      "id": "scopus_1237",
      "title": "Mid rise clt buildings - The UK's experience and potential for AUS and NZ",
      "authors": "Zumbrunnen, Philipp and Fovargue, Jonathan",
      "affiliations": "Eurban Limited, London, United Kingdom",
      "countries": [
        "United Kingdom"
      ],
      "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2012, WCTE 2012",
      "year": 2012,
      "score": 38,
      "abstract": "Over the last 20 years Cross laminated timber (CLT) has become a very successful engineered wood product in Central Europe. 10 years ago it was first used in the UK as roof elements to a conventional building and has grown to become an established building system within the UK's construction Industry. There are now over 100 CLT projects in the UK across all industry sectors. It has developed a special role within the mid rise residential sector, that has stimulated interest across the world. What are the reasons for this, and how has this building material attracted such interest from architects, contractors and their clients? This paper gives an overview of the history of the CLT in the UK, with a focus on the mid rise buildings from Eurban, one of the leading engineers and contractors of CLT in the UK. It will give also offer a view of the near future as CLT steps into UK's high rise sector and also the potential for its development in new markets in Australia and New Zealand.",
      "keywords": [
        "Architecture and structures",
        "Building structures",
