    {
      "id": "scopus_1034",
      "title": "Point-supported flat slabs with CLT panels",
      "authors": "Maurer, Bernhard and Maderebner, Roland and Zingerle, Philipp and Färberböck, Ingo and Flach, Michael",
      "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
      "countries": "País não informado",
      "journal": "WCTE 2018 - World Conference on Timber Engineering",
      "year": 2018,
      "score": 42,
      "abstract": "The paper shows a system solution for point-supported flat slabs made of cross-laminated timber without joists and span widths of minimum 5 m. The system solution contains a connector consisting of steel including self-tapping screws in order to reinforce the bearing area and the design of a stiff joint for the narrow side of CLT plates in form of dovetails made of polymer concrete. The paper focuses on the connector for the reinforcement of the bearing area and presents the results of experimental and numerical investigations of the carried out punching tests. A comparison with un-reinforced tests shows the potential in improving the load-carrying capacity of the bearing area of point-supported flat slabs made of cross-laminated timber. In addition, the results of the punching tests compared with FE-simulations concerning the rotational behavior in the bearing area are shown. © WCTE 2018 Committee.",
      "keywords": [
        "CLT",
        "Connector",
        "Joints",
        "Point-supported flat slab",
        "Punching tests"
      ],
