    {
      "id": "scopus_421",
      "title": "A shear connector for direction-independent shear force transmission in TCC slabs; Ein Verbundmittel zur richtungsunabhängigen Schubkraftübertragung in HBV-Decken",
      "authors": "Sorg, Christian and Kurz, Wolfgang and D'Escurac, Arnaud Pavis",
      "affiliations": "Rheinland-Pfälzische Technische Universität Kaiserslautern-Landau, Fachgebiet Stahlbau, Kaiserslautern, Rheinland-Pfalz, Germany; Werner Sobek Frankfurt GmbH & Co. KG, Frankfurt am Main, Germany",
      "countries": [
        "Germany"
      ],
      "journal": "Bautechnik",
      "year": 2023,
      "score": 49,
      "abstract": "A shear connector for direction-independent shear force transmission in TCC slabs. Currently used timber-concrete composite (TCC) slabs carry loads only in one direction, and notches or other shear connectors are used for shear force transmission. As a result, these slabs lack the flexibility and effectiveness as a two-way spanning, reinforced concrete flat slab. To overcome these limitations, a novel bi-axial spanning TCC slab is being developed. The investigation of this new system is part of a research project, carried out at the University of Kaiserslautern (TUK) in collaboration with Werner Sobek Frankfurt GmbH & Co. KG (WS Frankfurt). The connection of the two cross-sections is a key component in such systems. Therefore, developing a shear connector for direction-independent shear force transmission is an important aspect of this project. In this paper, the results of numerical and experimental investigations of the connection system (cylindrical concrete notch) are presented and discussed. The focus is on the stiffness and load-bearing capability as well as the structural behaviour. © 2023, Ernst und Sohn. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "cross-laminated timber",
        "cylindrical concrete notch",
        "flat slab",
        "Reinforced concrete construction",
        "Timber construction",
        "timber-concrete composite slabs",
        "two-way spanning slab"
      ],
      "studyType": "Article",
      "quality": null,
      "doi": "10.1002/bate.202200066",
      "language": "German",
      "source": "Scopus",
