    {
      "id": "scopus_286",
      "title": "SHEAR PERFORMANCE OF CLT-CONCRETE JOINT WITH INCLINED INSERTED LAG SCREWS IN THE DIRECTION OF TENSILE RESISTANCE; 引張抵抗方向への斜め挿入ラグスクリューによる CLT −コンクリート接合部の 1 面せん断性能",
      "authors": "Ohki, Fumiaki and Morohashi, Noritaka and Hiramatsu, Yasushi and Noda, Yasunobu and Miyatake, Atsushi and Suzuki, Kento",
      "affiliations": "FFPRI; Nihon University, Dept. of Architecture and Architectural Engineering, Tokyo, Japan",
      "countries": [
        "Japan"
      ],
      "journal": "AIJ Journal of Technology and Design",
      "year": 2024,
      "score": 53,
      "abstract": "A push-out test was conducted using specimens connecting cross laminated timber (CLT) and concrete with lag screws, inserted at an angle of 0°–60° in the direction of lag screw bearing tensile forces. The purpose of this test was to examine the effect of the insertion angle of lag screws, which are used as shear connectors in CLT–concrete composite slabs, on shear performance. The results showed that when the insertion angle was increased from 0° to 30°, the stiffness (slip modulus) increased and the yield as well as the maximum and ultimate loads tended to reach their maximum values. © 2024 Architectural Institute of Japan. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Composite slab",
        "Concrete",
        "Cross laminated timber (CLT)",
        "Inclined insertion",
        "Lag screw",
        "Shear performance"
      ],
