    {
      "id": "scopus_748",
      "title": "Structural availability of mixed CLT using red pine and yellow popular",
      "authors": "Kim, Keonho and Song, Dabin",
      "affiliations": "National Institute of Forest Science, Department of Forest Products, Jinju, South Korea",
      "countries": [
        "South Korea"
      ],
      "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2021, WCTE 2021",
      "year": 2021,
      "score": 62,
      "abstract": "Recently the CLT(cross laminated timber) is using as one of structural building materials in the high raised wooden building. When the CLT which is the engineered wood is used as shear wall or floors, the design value of CLT should be provided. To verify the structural availability of mixed CLT using the red-pine and yellow popular, the bending test under the 4 point loading was conducted. The mixed CLT was composed of 2 red pine laminae and a yellow popular. The red pine lamina as major axial layer was categorized by the machine grading. The yellow popular was the 3rd grade in visual grading based on the KS F 3020. In results of bending test, the bending MOE(modulus of elasticity) and MOR(modulus of rupture) of CLT increased by the MOE of red pine lamina. The MOR of mixed CLT was 1.33 times higher than the unmixed CLT composed by only red pine layers. The bending failure at the bottom major layer transferred to the rolling shear failure of minor layer. The bending performance of CLT was predicted by Shear Analogy Method. The predicted MOE was similar to the experiment MOE. © WCTE 2021. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Mixed CLT",
        "Modulus of elasticity",
        "Modulus of rupture",
        "Red pine",
        "Yellow popular"
      ],
