    {
      "id": "scopus_853",
      "title": "Development and verification of analytical method using fem for structural design to model out of plane bending behavior of two-way flat slab using CLT",
      "authors": "Esaka, Yoshisato and Murakami, Katsuhide and Mimatsu, Azusa and Honda, Sadamitsu and Shiozaki, Masao and Komatsu, Kenji and Murakami, Masahide and Inayama, Masahiro and Ida, Mari",
      "affiliations": "Nikken Sekkei Ltd., Department of Engineering, Tokyo, Japan; PAL Corporation, Structural R&D Dept.; Yamasa Mokuzai Co., Ltd., Department of Engineering, Kagoshima, Japan; Yamasa Mokuzai Co., Ltd., Kagoshima, Japan; Kindai University, Faculty of Architecture, Higashiosaka, Osaka, Japan; The University of Tokyo, School of Agricultural and Life Sciences, Tokyo, Japan",
      "countries": [
        "Japan"
      ],
      "journal": "AIJ Journal of Technology and Design",
      "year": 2020,
      "score": 65,
      "abstract": "Authors develop the two-way flat slab system that is layered CLTs so that the strong axial direction of CLT (Cross Laminated Timber) is orthogonal. GIR (Glued-in rod) joint system is used for joining between CLT. FEM analysis for two-way flat slab using CLT designs is made based on element experiments and the validity of the analysis is compared with keyed beam and several actual measurements of two-way flat slab using CLT in the building. © 2020 Architectural Institute of Japan. All rights reserved.",
