e bending strength in high axial force was underestimated especially in the latter, and that the expansion of compressive region from the axial force wasn’t appropriately estimated in these methods. Lastly, the load incremental analysis using the structural model with MS elements for 3-story CLT construction used in past shake table test was conducted. As a result, it was recognized that analytical relations between story shear and story drift well agreed with the result of shake table test, while analytical result using the standard structural model above mentioned underestimated the stiffness and the strength. The composition of MS element, that is composed with discrete spring elements corresponding to the edge of CLT panel and the tensile connection, isn’t simple. However, it is set between 2 nodes, and the force-deformation relations of each spring elements are automatically converted into the force-deformation relation of these nodes. Therefore, MS element can be dealt as the unitary element in the structural model for analysis, enabling simplification of the model. Besides, M-N interaction is appropriately estimated even in high axial force by MS element, therefore it is adequate also for structural design of high-rise building. MS element is planned to be added as one of the standard elements for structural model of CLT constructions in next revision of the manual above mentioned. © 2024, International Association for Earthquake Engineering. All rights reserved.",
