    {
      "id": "scopus_1033",
      "title": "Experimental performance of post-tensioned rocking single-panel CLT walls",
      "authors": "He, Minjuan and Sun, Xiaofeng and Li, Zheng",
      "affiliations": "Tongji University, Shanghai, China",
      "countries": [
        "China"
      ],
      "journal": "WCTE 2018 - World Conference on Timber Engineering",
      "year": 2018,
      "score": 72,
      "abstract": "The paper presents the experimental response of scaled post-tensioning rocking CLT shear walls under cyclic loading. A total of three two-storey and single-panel CLT shear walls with vertical post-tensioned steel strands were tested. The strands passed through the CLT panels and were anchored to the CLT panels at the top of the walls and to the foundation at the bottom of the walls. The post-tensioned rocking CLT walls tested incorporated the CLT floor diaphragm system and CLT wall panels. Creep deformation of the CLT floor diaphragms under long-term service would lead to the loss in the post-tensioning force, thus the CLT floor diaphragm system was specially designed to mitigate the creep deformation of the CLT floor diaphragms subjected to the perpendicular-to-grain compression. The influence of the applied initial post-tensioning force on the mechanical properties of the rocking shear walls was analyzed. In addition, the rocking deformation, the in-plane shear and flexural deformation of the tested wall panels under lateral loads were also investigated and reported. © WCTE 2018 Committee.",
      "keywords": [
        "Cross-laminated timber",
        "Mechanical properties",
        "Post-tensioning",
        "Rocking shear walls",
        "Shear and flexural deformation"
      ],
      "studyType": "Conference paper",
