    {
      "id": "scopus_48",
      "title": "Experimental study on long-term performance of pre-stressed cross-laminated timber shear walls; 预应力正交胶合木剪力墙长期性能试验研究",
      "authors": "Sun, Xiaofeng and Li, Shuanglun and He, Minjuan and Lei, Ying and Ou, Jiajia",
      "affiliations": "Xiamen University, School of Architecture and Civil Engineering, Xiamen, Fujian, China; Xiamen University, Xiamen, Fujian, China; Tongji University, Shanghai, China; State Key Laboratory of Disaster Reduction in Civil Engineering, Shanghai, China; Chengdu Aircraft Design and Research Institute, Chengdu, Sichuan, China",
      "countries": [
        "China"
      ],
      "journal": "Jianzhu Jiegou Xuebao/Journal of Building Structures",
      "year": 2025,
      "score": 91,
      "abstract": "Pre-stressed cross-laminated timber（CLT）shear walls have advantages such as good seismic resilience and high lateral load-bearing capacity. However，during their service lives，the long-term compression creep of CLT，along with the loss of effective tension in the steel strands，leads to a degradation in the lateral load resistance performance of the shear walls. To study the long-term deformation of pre-stressed CLT shear walls in natural environments and analyze the tension loss pattern，the pre-stressed CLT shear walls with and without CLT floor as well as one non-pre-stressed CLT shear wall for obtaining the CLT environmental deformation were arranged. A 450-day long-term performance test was conducted. Based on the collection of the environmental temperature and humidity，the CLT strain，the moisture content of CLT panels，and effective tension of steel strands，the moisture content fluctuation trends of CLT panels were analyzed and the coefficients of environmental strain of the CLT wall panels and those of the CLT floors were obtained. Additionally，the effective tension loss patterns of steel strands between the pre-stressed CLT shear wall with CLT floor and that without CLT floor were compared. The proportion of tension loss after a 50-year service period was estimated. The results show that the moisture content fluctuation trends at different depths of CLT panels are consistent with the variations of site humidity. When the initial moisture content is similar，the moisture content variation at shallower positions beneath the CLT surface is more significant. For the CLT wall panels and the CLT floors，the coefficients of environmental strain are recommended as 0. 027 4 and 0. 583 3， respectively. For the pre-stressed CLT shear wall with CLT floor and that without CLT floor， the effective tension of the steel strands after a 50-year service period is expected to decrease to 69% and 94% of the initial value， respectively. © 2025 Science Press. All rights reserved.",
      "keywords": [
        "Creep",
        "Loads (forces)",
        "Moisture",
        "Shear flow",
        "Shear walls",
        "Shearing",
        "Steel beams and girders",
        "%moisture",
        "Cross laminated",
        "Environmental strain",
        "Laminated timber",
        "Lateral loads",
        "Long term performance",
        "Loss patterns",
        "Pre-stressed",
        "Steel strand",
        "Wall panels",
        "Floors",
        "Moisture determination"
      ],
