          "abstract": "The proceedings contain 152 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Canadian Society of Civil Engineering. The topics include: Evaluation of Economically Optimal Seismic Retrofit Strategy for Highway Bridge Columns in High Seismic Regions in Canada; Experimental Behaviour of a Thermoplastic-FRP-Grid RC Slab; Decision Framework for the Evaluation of Wildfire Resilience and Sustainability in Single-Family Housing of British Columbia Interior (WiSE-BC); experimental Study on the Compressive and Diagonal Tensile Strengths of Full-Scale Concrete Masonry; Effect of Transverse Reinforcement on Bond Strength of Ribbed GFRP Bars in Concrete; Predictive Machine Learning Models for GFRP-Concrete Bond Strength; Crack Monitoring in GFRP-Reinforced Concrete Beams Using Digital Image Correlation; machine Learning Techniques for Analysing Post-tensioned Cross-Laminated Timber Behaviour Under Lateral Loads; Development of Live Load Moment and Tension Force in Bridge Deck Slab Overhang Due to Transverse Vehicle Impact for CHBDC 2025; measuring Strain Distributions in Curved Glulam Timber Beams Using Distributed Fibre Optic Sensors; comparison of Prefabricated Building Project Designs Based on Analysis of Floor Plan Drawings Using Deep Learning; performance Evaluation of Various Time Series Data Augmentation Techniques for Structural Vibration Application; seismic Response Analyses of Highway Bridges Designed with Extended Pile-Shafts; thermal Performance of Composite Insulation System Utilizing Cellulose and Aerogel Blankets for Modular Housing in Northern Canadian Regions; flexural Performance of Mechanically Laminated Timber Panels Under Concentrated Forces; exploring Interfaces in 3D-Printed Concrete Through Cohesive Zone Modelling; panelized Light-Frame Wood Roof as a Potential Housing Solution for Northern Canada; drone-Based 3D Model Reconstruction of Roadways: A Case Study.",
