        {
          "id": "scopus_210",
          "title": "Continuous Cross-Laminated Timber Concrete Composite Slim Floor System – Experimental Investigation; Durchlaufendes Brettsperrholz-Beton-Verbundsystem mit deckengleichen Stahlverbundtragern – Experimentelle Untersuchungen",
          "authors": "Rauber, Lukas and Theunissen, Emile and Walter, Burkhard and Hoffmeister, Benno",
          "affiliations": "Rheinisch-Westfälische Technische Hochschule Aachen, Fachgebiet Ingenieurholzbau, Aachen, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany; öbuvSV für Holzbau Walter + Reif Ingenieurgesellschaft GmbH, Aachen, Germany",
          "countries": [
            "Germany"
          ],
          "journal": "Bauingenieur",
          "year": 2025,
          "score": 14,
          "abstract": "The demand for timber-concrete composite floors (TCC floors) is increasing in the building sector. TCC combines the advantages of lightweight timber floors with the favorable structural properties of concrete floors. At present, single-span systems are mainly used; TCC continuous systems are still widely unconsidered in research and practice. This article presents experimental investigations on a multi-span slim floor TCC system. Cross-laminated timber elements with notches were combined with a concrete deck layer supported by steel concrete composite beams. The experiments were carried out on three levels: (i) notches; (ii) end and center supports and (iii) a two-span system. Notches and supports were analyzed with regard to their load-carrying properties (stiffness, load-carrying capacity, type of failure). For the two-span system, the timber moisture content, the dynamic properties and the deflections over the course of six months were investigated. The results show that it is essential to consider the load-carrying capacity and stiffness of the connections between TCC floor slabs and supporting beams in calculations. © 2025, VDI Fachmedien GmBH & Co. KG. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Concrete mixtures",
            "Concrete slabs",
            "Buildings sector",
            "Composite floors",
            "Cross laminated",
            "Experimental investigations",
            "Floor systems",
            "Laminated timber",
            "Load carrying",
            "Slim floor",
            "Timber floors",
            "Timber-concrete composites",
            "Architectural concrete"
          ],
