        {
          "id": "scopus_214",
          "title": "1st International Conference on Civil and Environmental Engineering for Resilient, Smart and Sustainable Solutions, 2024",
          "authors": "Autor não informado",
          "affiliations": "Afiliação não informada",
          "countries": "País não informado",
          "journal": "Materials Research Proceedings",
          "year": 2025,
          "score": 20,
          "abstract": "The proceedings contain 133 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Civil and Environmental Engineering for Resilient, Smart and Sustainable Solutions. The topics include: Evaluation of concrete slab exposed to weather conditions resulting from global warming; Shear capacity prediction of squat flanged walls using machine learning approach with CatBoost and CTGAN; Comprehensive analysis of structural beams: Theoretical calculations and simulation analysis using ANSYS; a modified design for improving pressure relief valve stability; site amplification using 1D seismic site response analysis in Islamabad: An application of building code of Pakistan 2021; critical building components analysis: An empirical study; Experimental study of BFRP-RC beams exposed to elevated temperatures; An optimization approach process of a 4-story RC building structural plan through generative design; Structural design analysis of hybrid multi-rise buildings, with CLT and LGS light weight floor system, at Neom-The Line; Sustainability and cost of a multi-story edifice, with CLT and LGS light weight floor system, at Neom-The Line; Seismic assessment of reinforced concrete building strengthened with CFRP sheets using non-linear static approach; cyclic performance of partially grouted reinforced masonry shear walls with boundary elements; a study case: Seismic evaluation of existing six-story office building with flat plate structural system; experimental evaluation of the masonry infilled reinforced concrete frame under reverse cyclic loading; comparative analysis of structural performance and cost efficiency of reinforced concrete and steel for a three-story warehouse in high-risk seismic zones; fire behaviour of mass timber beam-to-column hybrid connections-A state-of-the-art review; seismic assessment of masonry infilled frame structures.",
