        },
        {
          "id": "scopus_281",
          "title": "Study on single shear performance of notched connections of CLT⁃concrete composite floor in fire; 正交胶合木⁃混凝土组合楼板凹槽连接节点抗火性能研究",
          "authors": "Wang, Mingqian and Xu, Qingfeng and Song, Xiaobing and Chen, Lingzhu and Wang, Zhenpeng and Leng, Yubing",
          "affiliations": "Ltd., Shanghai, Shanghai, China; Shanghai Jiao Tong University, Shanghai, China",
          "countries": [
            "China"
          ],
          "journal": "Tumu Gongcheng Xuebao/China Civil Engineering Journal",
          "year": 2024,
          "score": 12,
          "abstract": "To investigate single shear performance of notched connections of CLT-concrete composite floor in fire, nine groups of specimens (27 in total) were designed and tested at normal temperature and in fire. Test results indicated that the screw drilling angle at normal temperature plays an important role in determining the typical failure modes of the specimens. The failure modes of the specimen groups subjected to fire for 90 minutes or less were similar, which shall be brittle shear failure of the concrete section near the notch. The failure modes of the specimen group exposed to fire for nearly 120 minutes shall be severe timber failure near the notch (including charring and falling off), longitudinal compressive yielding below the notch and concrete crushing failure neat the screw. With the gradual increase of the fire exposure time, the shear capacity of most specimen groups gradually decreases, and the maximum reduction is 28. 1%. The load ratio has an important influence on the fire resistance of the specimens. That is, with the continuous increase of the load ratio, the maximum decrease of the fire resistance of the specimens is 50. 7%. The simulation results of the finite element model, except for specimen groups SFL3 and SFL4, are relatively close to the test results for most cases, and the prediction error is within 15%, which may satisfy the engineering accuracy requirements. © 2024 Chinese Society of Civil Engineering. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "CLT-concrete composite floor",
            "fire condition",
            "notched connection",
            "numerical simulation",
            "single shear performance"
          ],
          "studyType": "Article",
          "quality": null,
          "doi": "10.15951/j.tmgcxb.22111147",
          "language": "Chinese",
          "source": "Scopus",
          "numString": 2,
          "isDuplicate": false,
