        {
          "id": "scopus_342",
          "title": "EFFECTS OF THE FLOOR-WALL INTERACTION ON THE POST-ELASTIC RESPONSE OF SEGMENTED CLT SHEAR WALLS",
          "authors": "D'Arenzo, Giuseppe and Seim, Werner",
          "affiliations": "Aarhus Universitet, Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering, Aarhus, Midtjylland, Denmark; Universität Kassel, Timber Structures and Building Rehabilitation, Kassel, Hessen, Germany",
          "countries": [
            "Denmark",
            "Germany"
          ],
          "journal": "World Conference on Earthquake Engineering proceedings",
          "year": 2024,
          "score": 22,
          "abstract": "This study investigates the impact of floor-wall interaction on the lateral response of Cross-Laminated Timber (CLT) segmented shear walls. A two-panel shear wall system was analyzed, considering various types of floor-to-wall connections typical in construction practice. Numerical analyses were conducted to replicate the full nonlinear behaviour of segmented shear walls. The results reveal that floor-wall interaction significantly alters the lateral behaviour of segmented shear walls, increasing stiffness and load-bearing capacity while decreasing deformation capacity. These variations are primarily associated with the type of floor-to-wall connection used. Specifically, connections with partially threaded screws measuring 10×260 mm spaced at 300mm resulted in a 27.4% and 28.0% increase in stiffness and strength, respectively, and a 36.8% decrease in deformation capacity. These modifications could influence the seismic behaviour and design of structures with segmented shear walls. The study underscores the importance of considering floor-wall interaction when assessing the lateral behaviour of multi-panel CLT shear walls. © 2024, International Association for Earthquake Engineering. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Earthquake effects",
            "Seismic design",
            "Shear walls",
            "Construction practice",
            "Cross laminated",
