        {
          "id": "scopus_601",
          "title": "Calculation method for shear capacity of cross-laminated timber wall-to-floor joints with angle steel bracket connections after fire; 正交胶合木墙体-楼板角撑连接节点受火后受剪承载力计算方法",
          "authors": "Zhang, Jin and Jiang, Kun and Lu, Chuan",
          "affiliations": "Key Laboratory of Concrete and Prestressed Concrete Structures, Ministry of Education, Nanjing, Jiangsu, China; Ltd., Nanchang, Jiangxi, China",
          "countries": [
            "China"
          ],
          "journal": "Dongnan Daxue Xuebao (Ziran Kexue Ban)/Journal of Southeast University (Natural Science Edition)",
          "year": 2022,
          "score": 21,
          "abstract": "To study the calculation method for the shear capacity of cross-laminated timber(CLT) wall-to-floor joints with angle steel bracket connections after fire, shear tests at normal temperature and the ones after fire were carried out on joints with the self-tapping screw length of 60 and 80 mm, respectively. Based on the calculation method for the shear capacity of CLT laminate pin shaft fasteners at normal temperature, the calculation method for the shear capacity of joints after fire was proposed considering the reduction of the bending strength of the steel pin and the effective bearing section of CLT laminates. The results show that for the normal temperature specimens, when the length of self-tapping screw increases from 60 to 80 mm, the yield load increases 1.51 times and the ductility coefficient decreases 0.77 times. For the specimens subjected to fire for 20 min, the increase of the length of self-tapping screw is basically ineffective to the increase of the yield load, and the ductility coefficient is almost unchanged. The shear capacity calculated by the calculation method is in good agreement with the test results, thus proving the correctness and applicability of the proposed method. © 2022, Editorial Department of Journal of Southeast University. All right reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross-laminated timber(CLT)",
            "Fire test",
            "Shear capacity",
            "Shear test",
            "Wall-to-floor joints with angle steel bracket connections"
          ],
          "studyType": "Article",
