        },
        {
          "id": "scopus_625",
          "title": "PRELIMINARY STUDY ON THE FLANKING TRANSMISSION OF THE CLT BUILDING BY USING SMALL CROSS- AND T-JUNCTION TEST SPECIMENS; 小型 T 字・十字型接合部試験体による CLT パネル工法建築物の側路伝搬音の影響に関する基礎的検討",
          "authors": "Hirakawa, Susumu and Hiramitsu, Atsuo",
          "affiliations": "Building Research Institute, Department of Environmental Engineering, not available, Japan; Japan National Institute for Land and Infrastructure Management, Building Dept., Tsukuba, Ibaraki, Japan",
          "countries": [
            "Japan"
          ],
          "journal": "Journal of Environmental Engineering (Japan)",
          "year": 2022,
          "score": 12,
          "abstract": "This paper investigated the effect of flanking transmission in the CLT building by using small cross- and T-junction test specimens from two aspects: 1. The measurement of the vibration level reduction (K<inf>ij</inf>) through the junctions are considered using small test specimens. The K<inf>ij</inf> is an index that allows the calculation of the coupling loss factor (η<inf>ij</inf>) for SEA based prediction models (i.e., ISO 12354-2:2017, impedance model and Transient SEA) and can be used to quantify the vibration transmissivity. 2. The theoretical estimation of K<inf>ij</inf> for Rigid T- and cross-junctions made by CLT panels were investigated. © 2022 Journal of Environmental Engineering (Japan). All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross Laminated Timber",
            "Flanking transmission",
            "Floor impact sound"
          ],
          "studyType": "Article",
          "quality": null,
          "doi": "10.3130/AIJE.87.371",
          "language": "English",
          "source": "Scopus",
          "numString": 2,
