        {
          "id": "scopus_765",
          "title": "Analysis model to predict in-plane performance of CLT floor composed with metal plate and spline",
          "authors": "Suzuki, Kento and Noda, Yasunobu and Ido, Hirofumi and Sugimoto, Kenichi",
          "affiliations": "Forestry and Forest Products Research Institute, Tsukuba, Ibaraki, Japan",
          "countries": [
            "Japan"
          ],
          "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2021, WCTE 2021",
          "year": 2021,
          "score": 25,
          "abstract": "Joint tests were conducted, and an analytical model that can predict in-plane performance was proposed for a Japanese CLT floor. In the joint tests, the structural performances of the joints constituting the CLT floor were confirmed. An analysis model was proposed assuming in-plane stresses on the CLT floor subjected to lateral load. The analysis model is simplified by converting the tension and compression elements into rotating springs. The analysis result was able to accurately predict the result of the full-scale lateral loading test of the CLT floor. © WCTE 2021. All rights reserved.",
