        {
          "id": "scopus_766",
          "title": "Development of span tables for mass timber panel-concrete composite floors",
          "authors": "Mirdad, Md Abdul Hamid and Li, Jialin and Chui, Yinghei",
          "affiliations": "University of Alberta, Edmonton, AB, Canada",
          "countries": [
            "Canada"
          ],
          "journal": "World Conference on Timber Engineering 2021, WCTE 2021",
          "year": 2021,
          "score": 18,
          "abstract": "Lack of design standard and guideline is the most important barrier for the widespread use of Mass Timber Panel-Concrete (MTPC) composite floor system in North America. The commonly used Gamma method to design timber-concrete composite floor has some limitations and cannot predict the capacity and ultimate failure modes of the composite system. An analytical model has been developed that accounts for the interlayer connection behaviour, including an acoustic layer between timber and concrete, to accurately predict the effective bending stiffness, capacity, and failure modes of MTPC composite floor system. In this paper it was demonstrated how the developed floor model can be used to generate allowable floor spans. To that end a floor span table for MTPC composite floors has been developed. The development of the span table considers strength limit states, deflection, vibration serviceability, acoustics, and fire resistance requirements. The span table will facilitate the use this type of composite floor system in mass timber construction. © WCTE 2021. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross laminated timber",
            "Glue laminated timber",
            "Mass timber panel",
            "Self-tapping screw",
            "Span table",
            "Timber-Concrete composite floor"
          ],
