        {
          "id": "scopus_818",
          "title": "Experimental study on floor impact sound reduction by double ceiling system with cross laminated timber panels",
          "authors": "Kasai, Yusuke and Tanaka, Manabu and Murakami, Tsuyoshi",
          "affiliations": "General Building Research Corporation of Japan, Suita, Osaka, Japan",
          "countries": [
            "Japan"
          ],
          "journal": "Proceedings of 2020 International Congress on Noise Control Engineering, INTER-NOISE 2020",
          "year": 2020,
          "score": 33,
          "abstract": "One of the characteristics of Cross laminated timber (=CLT) is its lightness compared to concrete, but this may be disadvantageous in terms of sound insulation. Therefore, in order to use CLT panels as floor slabs, it is required to improve impact sound insulation performance. For the purpose of improving impact sound insulation performance, the authors conducted laboratory measurements of test specimens with several variations of CLT double ceiling system adding to CLT floor slabs. First, adding a double ceiling with a closed air back cavity improved only light floor impact sound insulation performance. In case of its air back cavity opened to the sound receiving room, both heavy/soft and light floor impact sound levels became higher. On the other hand, when the thickness of the air back cavity was increased and a clearance of its air back cavity opened to horizontal direction, heavy/soft floor impact sound insulation performance was improved. Further, by increasing the thickness of the air back cavity while leaving a clearance in the horizontal direction and loading weights of sand bags on CLT ceiling panels, heavy/soft floor impact sound insulation performance greatly improved from the specification without CLT panel double ceiling system. © Proceedings of 2020 International Congress on Noise Control Engineering, INTER-NOISE 2020. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Acoustic noise",
            "Acoustic variables control",
            "Ceilings",
            "Electric circuit breakers",
            "Floors",
            "Laminating",
            "Sound insulating materials",
            "Timber",
            "Back cavities",
            "Ceiling systems",
            "Cross laminated",
