        {
          "id": "scopus_888",
          "title": "Proposal for standard test method to evaluate the performance of cross-laminated timber exposed to fire; Vorschlag einer Standardprüfmethode für Brettsperrholz im Brandfall",
          "authors": "Klippel, Michael and Schmid, Joachim and Fahrni, Reto and Kleinhenz, Miriam and Frangi, Andrea",
          "affiliations": "ETH Zürich, Zurich, ZH, Switzerland",
          "countries": [
            "Switzerland"
          ],
          "journal": "Bautechnik",
          "year": 2019,
          "score": 22,
          "abstract": "Proposal for standard test method to evaluate the performance of cross-laminated timber exposed to fire. In recent years, cross-laminated timber (CLT) has become a popular wood-based product for high quality and innovative timber construction. As with any building product, the fire performance and fire resistance of CLT elements must be carefully assessed when designing buildings. The adhesive used in the glueline of CLT plays an important role in the fire design. However, at present, the European standards do not provide a test method to assess the adhesive properties in CLT exposed to fire. At ETH Zurich, fire tests were carried out with CLT floor elements in which adhesives with various properties were tested in fire. This article presents the results of these fire tests and shows a possible European test method for the classification of adhesives. It is shown that the mass loss of the CLT elements during an EN/ISO standard fire can be used to evaluate the integrity of the surface gluing in fire. © 2019, Ernst und Sohn. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "adhesive",
            "classification",
            "cross-laminated timber",
            "design",
            "fire",
            "Fire protection",
            "fire test",
            "Timber construction",
            "timber structures"
          ],
