        {
          "id": "scopus_940",
          "title": "Floor impact sound insulation of the six-story wood-frame model building",
          "authors": "Hiramitsu, Atsuo and Tomita, Ryuta and Hirakawa, Susumu and Sato, Masayoshi",
          "affiliations": "Japan National Institute for Land and Infrastructure Management, Tsukuba, Ibaraki, Japan; Nihon University, Tokyo, Japan; Building Research Institute, Tsukuba, Ibaraki, Japan; Japan 2x4 Home Builders Association, Tokyo, Japan",
          "countries": [
            "Japan"
          ],
          "journal": "Proceedings of the International Congress on Acoustics",
          "year": 2019,
          "score": 27,
          "abstract": "In Japan, the Act for Promotion of Use of Wood in Public Buildings was enforced in 2010. As a result, the number of constructions using the timber structure became more popular for the buildings. However, the performance of the floor impact sound insulation in the timber construction buildings is often concerned as worse than the concrete constructions. In this paper, an experiments were carried out on a newly built six-story wood-frame building to investigate the performance of the floor impact sound insulation on five different floors; CLT panel floor, stressed skin panel floor, LVL floor, I-joist floor and chord truss floor. The result showed that the stressed skins panel floor has the highest performance of heavy-weight floor impact sound insulation. The paper also reports the sound insulation of separation wall and the vibration performance in the timber construction building, and proposes an improvement plan for the better floor impact and airborne sound insulation performance in the timber construction buildings. © 2019 Proceedings of the International Congress on Acoustics. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross Laminated Timber",
            "Floor impact sound insulation",
            "Wood-frame construction"
          ],
          "studyType": "Conference paper",
