        {
          "id": "scopus_1086",
          "title": "Cross-laminated timber panels for slabs: Mechanical experimental evaluation under different consumption of adhesive levels; Painéis de madeira laminada colada cruzada para lajes: Avaliação experimental mecânica sob diferentes níveis de consumo de adesivo",
          "authors": "Ecker, Taienne Winni Paiz and Miotto, José Luiz and Turmina, Gabriel",
          "affiliations": "União de Ensino do Sudoeste do Paraná - UNISEP, PR, Brazil; Universidade Estadual de Maringá, Maringa, PR, Brazil",
          "countries": [
            "Brazil"
          ],
          "journal": "Ciencia y Engenharia/ Science and Engineering Journal",
          "year": 2017,
          "score": 17,
          "abstract": "The construction system in cross-laminated timber (CLT) is seen as a new concept for structural engineering, due to its high pre-fabrication level, reduced construction time and the possibility of multi-floor constructions. In addition, CLT panels are made of renewable material and promote constructions with lower waste generation, contributing to sustainable development. However, being a recent product, it is essential to carry out studies related to its structural performance. Therefore, this paper presents the results obtained in bending tests of CLT panels for slabs, formed by three orthogonal layers of pinus lamellae, bonded by monocomponent polyurethane adhesive. In order to evaluate the bonding efficiency of adhesive, twelve panels were produced with different quantities of adhesives: 120 g/m<sup>2</sup>, 160 g/m<sup>2</sup> and 200 g/m<sup>2</sup>. The panels produced with 200 g/m<sup>2</sup> of adhesive showed better performance, with average values of 34.21 MPa for the modulus of rupture and 10,200 MPa for the modulus of elasticity, similar to those required by ANSI/APA PRG 320: 2012, which shows the influence of the amount of adhesive applied on the mechanical performance of the panels.",
          "keywords": [
            "Bending test",
            "Cross laminated timber",
            "Polyurethane adhesive"
          ],
