          "year": 2013,
          "score": 5,
          "abstract": "As early as 1970, the structural engineering and building safety community recognized that a large number of two-, three-and four-story woodframe buildings designed with the first floor used either for parking or commercial space were built with readily identifiable structural system deficiencies, referred to as a",
