        },
        {
          "id": "scopus_1233",
          "title": "Vibrations of timber floor beams with end restraints",
          "authors": "Malo, Kjell Arne and Köhler, Jochen",
          "affiliations": "Norges Teknisk-Naturvitenskapelige Universitet, Trondheim, Trondelag, Norway",
          "countries": [
            "Norway"
          ],
          "journal": "Structures and Architecture: Concepts, Applications and Challenges - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Structures and Architecture, ICSA 2013",
          "year": 2013,
          "score": 10,
          "abstract": "Floors of cross-laminated timber are often installed in-between the vertical wall elements, leading to rotational restraints at the boundaries. New fastening techniques based on screws and threaded rods make it more convenient to use floor beam systems with end restraints. Improved structural stiffness of the floor structures may be gained. This has a positive influence on the vibrational performance of timber based floors. The paper aims at a simplified quantification of the effect of end restraints with respect to the vibrational performance. © 2013 Taylor & Francis Group.",
