        {
          "id": "scopus_1275",
          "title": "The",
          "authors": "Follesa, Maurizio and Lavisci, Paolo and Esposito, Vincenzo and Panerai, Lorenzo and Barone, Marco and Celli, Daniel and Cappelli, Stefano",
          "affiliations": "Timber Engineering, Florence, Italy; Legnopiù Srl, Prato, Italy; HYDEA S.p.A., Florence, Italy",
          "countries": [
            "Italy"
          ],
          "journal": "11th World Conference on Timber Engineering 2010, WCTE 2010",
          "year": 2010,
          "score": 1,
          "abstract": "Following the sustainability policies of the Regional Council of Tuscany, Casa SPA a public Company located in Florence which is in Charge of designing, constructing and maintaining the social housing real estate of the whole Florentine area, started a project which will lead to the construction in a central area of Florence of three multi-storey buildings, one of which is a six storey building, which will be entirely constructed using timber load bearing structures with the cross-laminated panel system. Particularly, the six storey building, which will be totally constructed with timber cross-laminated panels as bearing structures, including walls, floors, and all stair and lift cores, will be the first pioneer construction of such a tall residential timber building in a seismic area in Italy. In this paper the details of the project are presented, focusing particularly on the architectural, structural and sustainability issues. The construction will start in summer 2010.",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross laminated timber",
            "Multi-storey buildings",
            "Social housing"
          ],
