        {
          "id": "web_of_science_1317",
          "title": "Dynamic response of CLT plate systems in the context of timber and hybrid construction",
          "authors": "Weckendorf, Jan and Ussher, Ebenezer and Smith, Ian",
          "affiliations": "University of New Brunswick",
          "countries": [],
          "journal": "COMPOSITE STRUCTURES",
          "year": 2016,
          "score": 7,
          "abstract": "An experimental investigation of low amplitude dynamic responses of cross-laminated-timber (CLT) floors is presented to illuminate effects of variables like plan aspect ratio, support conditions and CLT type. Data extraction and analysis focus on determination of modal frequencies and damping. Practical implications of results are discussed in the context of vibration serviceability. (C) 2016 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
