        {
          "id": "web_of_science_1591",
          "title": "Seismic Fragility Estimates for Cross-Laminated Timber Platform Building",
          "authors": "Shahnewaz, Md and Pan, Yuxin and Alam, M. Shahria and Tannert, Thomas",
          "affiliations": "University of Northern British Columbia; University of British Columbia",
          "countries": [],
          "journal": "JOURNAL OF STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING",
          "year": 2020,
          "score": 15,
          "abstract": "Cross-laminated timber (CLT) has been gaining popularity also in seismic regions, because of its low carbon footprint and potential cost-competitiveness with concrete and steel construction. Recent effort has focused on developing standardized design provisions for CLT buildings. In the study presented herein, incremental dynamic analysis (IDA) was performed on a six-story CLT platform-type building. A nonlinear numerical model was developed in OpenSees considering the CLT shear walls as elastic shell elements and the con-nections (wall-to-foundation, wall-to-floor, and wall-to-wall) as nonlinear springs. The hysteresis behavior of the connections was modeled using ``pinching4''",
          "keywords": [
            "Mass-timber construction",
            "Finite element analyses",
            "Incremental dynamic analysis"
          ],
          "studyType": "Article",
          "quality": null,
