        {
          "id": "web_of_science_1968",
          "title": "Timber T-section beams: From pre-tensioning to self-tensioning",
          "authors": "Estevez-Cimadevila, J. and Otero-Chans, D. and Martin-Gutierrez, E. and Suarez-Riestra, F. and Vazquez-Rodriguez, J.",
          "affiliations": "Estévez-Cimadevila, J (Corresponding Author), Univ A Coron, Grp Architecton Struct, A Corona, Spain. Estevez-Cimadevila, J.; Otero-Chans, D.; Martin-Gutierrez, E.; Suarez-Riestra, F.; Vazquez-Rodriguez, J., Univ A Coron, Grp Architecton Struct, A Corona, Spain.",
          "countries": [
            "Spain"
          ],
          "journal": "STRUCTURES AND ARCHITECTURE: BRIDGING THE GAP AND CROSSING BORDERS",
          "year": 2019,
          "score": 4,
          "abstract": "A comparative bending behaviour analysis of timber T-section beams, in untensioned, pre-tensioned and self-tensioned conditions was carried out. Their T-section was composed of a glulam Picea abies or Oak web and an upper CLT flange. Twenty-four 9 m span specimens were tested until failure. Self-tensioning used a patented system (SsS (c)) based on a device composed of articulated rods that is anchored to the supports of the beams and connected to a non-adherent tendon. Although pre-tensioning the T-sections significantly increases their load-bearing capacity, this is not significant because the dimensions of simply supported beams are not usually determined by their ultimate limit state but by their serviceability limit state. Results show that pre-tensioning slightly varied stiffness because of the increased compression area. The results of self-tensioning specimens show a significant improvement in their behavior at the serviceability limit state. Consequently the proposed system is considered to be especially suitable for use with long-span wooden structural floors.",
          "keywords": [],
          "studyType": "Proceedings Paper",
          "quality": null,
          "doi": null,
          "language": "English",
          "source": "Web of Science",
          "numString": 3,
          "isDuplicate": false,
          "duplicateOf": null,
          "dataProcessingStatus": "pending",
