          "lastModified": "2026-02-23T22:37:42.910Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "scopus_2023",
          "title": "Acoustic emission monitoring of cross-laminated timber-steel composite beams during elastic bending",
          "authors": "Manthei, Gerd and Bohn, Dennis and Böhm, Noah and Kühn, Bertram and Vogelsberg, Achim",
          "affiliations": "Technische Hochschule Mittelhessen, Giessen, Hessen, Germany",
          "countries": [
            "Germany"
          ],
          "journal": "11th European Workshop on Structural Health Monitoring, EWSHM 2024",
          "year": 2024,
          "score": 24,
          "abstract": "Reinforcement of cross-laminated timber floors by a composite design with steel girders can provide an innovative and sustainable alternative for highly stressable floor systems made of steel and concrete for spans exceeding 8 m. To make this construction method economical and resource efficient, a significant contribution of the cross-laminated timber panel to the composite stiffness is necessary. One key aspect of the composite design is the formation of the shear-resistant connection between CLT panel and steel girder. The effect of both composites on the bending stiffness of cross laminated timber -steel composite beams was investigated in large-scale 4-point bending tests with span up to 10.6 m. To monitor the damage of the specimen using acoustic emission analysis, a network with 16 AE sensors were attached to the surface of the specimen in an area of largest deflection and highest load. For this purpose, broadband AE sensors with a measurement frequency of up to 200 kHz were used. The ultimate failure of the specimen with a span of 10.6 m occurred at a maximum test load of approximately 210 kN. The largest deflection at this force was about 214 mm. During two tests, which lasted about 50 minutes, 8,537 and 6,628 AE events were detected, respectively. The AE activity increases progressively from 30% of the maximum force until the specimens fail. © 2024 11th European Workshop on Structural Health Monitoring, EWSHM 2024. All rights reserved.",
          "keywords": [
            "acoustic emission analysis",
            "bending stiffness",
            "cross-laminated timber",
            "steel-timber-composite",
            "wood composites"
          ],
          "studyType": "Conference paper",
          "quality": null,
          "doi": "10.58286/29578",
