        {
          "id": "scopus_2064",
          "title": "Moment and shear capacity of Ply-lam composed with plywood and structural timber under out-of-plane bending",
          "authors": "Pang, Sung Jun and Lee, Hyeon-jeong and Yang, Seungmin and Kang, Seoggoo and Oh, Jung Kwon",
          "affiliations": "Research Institute of Agricultural and Life Science, Seoul, South Korea; Seoul National University, Department of Forest Sciences, Seoul, South Korea; Chungnam National University, Department of Biobased Materials, Daejeon, South Korea; Research Institute of Agricultural and Life Science, Department of Forest Sciences, Seoul, South Korea",
          "countries": [
            "South Korea"
          ],
          "journal": "Journal of Wood Science",
          "year": 2019,
          "score": 20,
          "abstract": "The aim of this study was to investigate the moment and shear capacity of Ply-lam which is composed with plywood and structural timber. The moment and shear capacity of Ply-lam were predicted by using prediction methodologies for typical cross-laminated timber (CLT). The predicted values by the methodologies were verified by comparison with measured capacities. Fifty-eight specimens of Ply-lam (five layers) were manufactured and half of the specimens were tested for bending (span-to-depth ratio (R<inf>sd</inf>) was 25:1). The other specimens were tested for rolling shear (R<inf>sd</inf> was 12:1) in accordance with EN 16351. The results show that typical prediction methods for structural properties of CLT can also be used to predict those of Ply-lam, since the measured values were higher than the predicted values. In rolling shear test, 52% specimens failed by bending at the bottom layer. This indicates that the rolling shear test method in EN 16351 was not suitable for Ply-lam because the typical CLT would be reinforced by replacing the cross layer with plywood. Thus, the span-to-depth ratio needs to be reduced for hybrid CLT like Ply-lam. © 2019, The Author(s).",
          "keywords": [
            "Cross-laminated timber",
            "Moment capacity",
            "Ply-lam",
            "Plywood",
            "Shear capacity",
            "Structural timber"
          ],
