        {
          "id": "web_of_science_2118",
          "title": "Bending performance of cross-laminated timber reinforced with glass fibre-reinforced polymer and aluminium sheets",
          "authors": "Rostampour-Haftkhani, Akbar and Abdoli, Farshid and Hajializadeh, Farajolah and Rashidi, Maria and Nasir, Vahid",
          "affiliations": "University of Mohaghegh Ardabili; Western Sydney University; Western Sydney University; Oregon State University; University of British Columbia",
          "countries": [],
          "journal": "INTERNATIONAL WOOD PRODUCTS JOURNAL",
          "year": 2025,
          "score": 50,
          "abstract": "There is limited research on enhancing the flexural performance of cross-laminated timber (CLT) panels made from fast-growing hardwood species like poplar, particularly using external reinforcements. This study aims to investigate the effect of aluminium (AL) and glass fibre-reinforced polymer (GFRP) sheets on the bending behaviour of 3-ply poplar CLT panels in both longitudinal (L) and transverse (T) directions. Four reinforcement configurations were tested. The results showed that AL reinforcement increased MOR by 53.9\\% (L) and 208\\% (T), and MOE by 56.9\\% (L) and 617\\% (T) of CLT samples. GFRP led to MOR gains of 37.4\\% (L) and 61.8\\% (T), and MOE gains of 38.3\\% (L) and 223\\% (T) in CLT samples. The most effective flexural performance in CLT samples was achieved with three layers of reinforcement, particularly with AL. Ductility of CLT samples also improved significantly: AL increased it by 76.6\\% (L) and 28\\% (T), while GFRP improved it by 47\\% (L) and 55\\% (T). These findings suggest that external reinforcement - especially with AL - can effectively enhance bending performance and ductility of poplar CLT, providing a viable strategy to improve its structural performance for broader application in engineered timber construction.",
          "keywords": [
            "cross-laminated timber (CLT)",
            "poplar",
            "CLT reinforcement",
            "GFRP",
            "MOE",
            "MOR"
          ],
          "studyType": "Article",
          "quality": null,
          "doi": "10.1177/20426445251362979",
          "language": "English",
          "source": "Web of Science",
          "numString": 6,
          "isDuplicate": false,
          "duplicateOf": null,
          "dataProcessingStatus": "pending",
